    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n622" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Actor</span></b> , ŏris, m. <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<i>A companion of Aeneas</i>, <i><span class="en">Verg. A. 9,
				500</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<i>An Auruncan</i>, <i><span class="en">ib. 12,
			94</span></i>; <i><span class="en">96</span></i>.—Hence, <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Actŏ-rĭdes</span></b> ,
			ae, patron. m., <i>son</i>
			or <i>grandson of Actor: his son</i>, <i>Menoetius</i>, <i><span class="en">Ov. F. 2, 39</span></i>; <i>his
				grandson</i>, <i>Patroclus</i>, <i><span class="en">Ov. Tr. 1,
				9, 29</span></i>; <i><span class="en">id. M. 13, 273</span></i>; <i>Erithos</i>, <i><span class="en">id. ib. 5, 79</span></i>.—In
				plur.: <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Actŏrĭdae</span></b> , i. e. <i>Eurytus and Cleatus</i>, <i>sons of Actor</i>,
				<i>King of Phthia</i>, <i><span class="en">id. ib. 8,
				308</span></i>.</div>
